  "result": "Perfect! All 288 tests pass. The mergeCustomers function is complete and working correctly.\n\n**mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)** \u2014 consolidates duplicate customers:\n- Returns `{ ok: true, value: { customers, invoices } }` where:\n  - The fromId customer is removed from the customers array\n  - All invoices referencing fromId now reference intoId\n  - Both customers and invoices are returned as copies (immutable)\n- Returns `{ ok: false, error: 'SAME_CUSTOMER' }` if both IDs reference the same customer\n- Returns `{ ok: false, error: 'CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND' }` if either ID doesn't exist\n- Handles case-insensitive ID matching via normalizeId()\n- Preserves all other invoice data during reassignment\n- Never mutates the original arrays\n\n**Tests cover:** customer removal, invoice reassignment, error handling (SAME_CUSTOMER, CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for fromId and intoId), case-insensitive ID matching, immutability of originals, data preservation, empty invoices, multiple invoices per customer, and preserving invoices from other customers.",
